Subject: [PATCH] remoteproc: qcom: use PAS authentication for IPQ5332 UserPDs

The IPQ5332 WCSS UserPD path uses PAS authentication and shutdown for
each user process, with the ASID-derived PAS identifier. Qualcomm's
downstream driver performs PAS_AUTH_AND_RESET before spawning a UserPD
and PAS_SHUTDOWN when stopping it.

MSA lock/unlock are different secure monitor operations and cannot
substitute for PIL authentication. In particular, an unavailable MSA
command may return success without configuring UserPD access. This
lets the DSP boot but fault on its first external DDR accesses.

Use the existing one-argument PAS services; downstream's additional
zero debug/reset arguments do not alter the underlying SCM request.

---
diff --git a/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_mpd.c b/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_mpd.c
--- a/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_mpd.c
+++ b/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_mpd.c
@@ -161,7 +161,7 @@
 	u32 pasid = (upd->pd_asid << 8) | UPD_SWID;
 	int ret;
 
-	ret = qcom_scm_msa_lock(pasid);
+	ret = qcom_scm_pas_auth_and_reset(pasid);
 	if (ret) {
 		dev_err(upd->dev, "failed to power up pd\n");
 		return ret;
@@ -232,7 +232,7 @@
 		}
 	}
 
-	ret = qcom_scm_msa_unlock(pasid);
+	ret = qcom_scm_pas_shutdown(pasid);
 	if (ret) {
 		dev_err(upd->dev, "failed to power down pd\n");
 		return ret;
